cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use genome_comparator, please cite it as below, together with Mash."
title: "genome_comparator: fast comparison and visualization of genome distances with Mash"
type: software
abstract: >-
  genome_comparator quickly compares and visualizes distances between genomes, from assemblies (fasta) or raw
  sequencing reads (fastq). It uses Mash to compute pairwise distances, then builds a distance matrix,
  UPGMA, neighbour joining and minimum evolution trees with optional bootstrap support, and an interactive
  principal coordinates analysis (PCoA) plot. It scales to thousands of genomes: sketches are computed in parallel
  and reused between runs.
